{"metadata":{"description":"Codex-style cross-task coordination for DeepSeek Harness: list, inspect, spawn, message and steer top-level sessions from a supervisor agent.","id":"gh:1356692170","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-plugin-task-coordinator","slug":"Kayungko/dsh-plugin-task-coordinator","topics":["dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Codex-style cross-task coordination for DeepSeek Harness: list, inspect, spawn, message and steer to"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"p-level sessions from a supervisor agent."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"**Codex-style cross-task coordination · a supervisor plugin for DeepSeek Harness**"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"What is this · Screenshots · Quick start · Tools · Architecture · Host contract · Web bridge (zh) · "},{"id":"p3s2","text":"enshots · Quick start · Tools · Architecture · Host contract · Web bridge (zh) · Changelog · Chinese"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"## What is this"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"**Once installed, you just say what should run in parallel — the `task_*` tools handle every step of"},{"id":"p5s2","text":" the orchestration:**"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"What happens behind the scenes: you (plain language) → supervisor session → decomposition analysis →"},{"id":"p7s2","text":" **an approval card you confirm** → batch-spawned task sessions → each task reports its result back "},{"id":"p7s3","text":"when done → the supervisor summarizes. You never watch a single step in between, but the decision po"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"ints stay in your hands."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"- This is a DSH plugin: **any top-level session** can discover tasks, read progress, spawn tasks and"},{"id":"p8s2","text":" deliver instructions;
- Spawned tasks **appear in the GUI session list immediately** (the same `api"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"-session/added` event the sidebar consumes);
- Every cross-task message is stamped with a `coordinat"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"or` source — visible and attributable in the target session's transcript;
- One prerequisite: **DSH "},{"id":"p8s5","text":"Desktop is installed and starts** (the plugin never launches the host for you)."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"> 📌 Host contract verified on **DSH 0.1.2-alpha.1**; every capability passed real-host end-to-end te"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"sting after restart (criteria in Host contract)."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Screenshots"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Live GUI captures — the same four shots are declared in screenshots.json for the dsh-market detail v"},{"id":"p11s2","text":" GUI captures — the same four shots are declared in screenshots.json for the dsh-market detail view."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"### Prerequisites"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"- DSH Desktop (contract verified on 0.1.2-alpha.1);
- Node.js `^22.19.0 || >=24` (the host runtime u"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"sually satisfies this already);
- PowerShell (the deploy script is `.ps1`)."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"### Install (one command)"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"> 🛒 **Listed on awesome-dsh-plugin (Workflow & Automation)** — with the in-app dsh-market plugin bro"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"wser, search “task-coordinator” and install/upgrade with one click. The git-clone route below is the"},{"id":"p16s3","text":" no-market equivalent."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"The script does three things: copies the plugin into the profile's `node_modules/` (no `pnpm install"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"`, the lockfile stays untouched), registers the dependency + bundle in the profile manifest, and upd"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"ates `.package-map.json` — **everything is backed up first** into `backups/<timestamp>/`."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"**Restart DSH Desktop** afterwards — any session can then use the eleven tools and the `/tasks` comm"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"start DSH Desktop** afterwards — any session can then use the eleven tools and the `/tasks` command."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"> 💡 `install.ps1` defaults `-Source` to `$PSScriptRoot/plugin` (workspace layout); when running from"},{"id":"p20s2","text":" the plugin repo itself, **pass `-Source .` explicitly**.
> Re-running is safe: file copies are idem"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"potent and manifest registration de-duplicates."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"### Verify"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"After the restart, send this to any session:"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"`List the currently visible tasks`"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"It calls `task_list` and returns the task list (an empty list is a valid answer) — the tools are mou"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"ls `task_list` and returns the task list (an empty list is a valid answer) — the tools are mounted ✅"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Uninstall: `pwsh install.ps1 -Source . -Uninstall` (also takes effect after restart)."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Directing the supervisor (prompting that actually works)"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"The model only coordinates when it can map your words to the tools. Vague prompts like "you may use "},{"id":"p27s2","text":"the /task plugin whenever you want" are discretionary — sessions tend to default to working solo (fi"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"eld-verified failure mode). Two rules:"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"1. **Name the tools, use imperative mood.** Example: "Split the remaining work with `task_spawn_batc"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"h` into parallel sub-task sessions (give them a team name); collect results with `task_wait`. Don't "},{"id":"p28s3","text":"do everything in this session."
2. **In /goal mode the coordination mandate must live inside the goa"},{"id":"p28s4","text":"l objective** — every continuation round re-anchors on that text alone. Recommended objective:"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"> As the supervisor session, take over the remaining development: ① splittable work MUST be dispatch"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"ed to parallel sub-task sessions via task_spawn_batch (attach a team name) — do not do everything yo"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"urself; ② collect results with task_wait and integrate them; ③ sub-task sessions may further paralle"},{"id":"p29s4","text":"lize with their own subagents; ④ push to remote main at every milestone."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"Loose wordings ("/task plugin", "coordinate things") are recognized too — the bundled skill carries "},{"id":"p30s2","text":"an alias table and the tool descriptions carry trigger context since 0.9.0 — but the imperative temp"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"late above is the reliable form, especially for goal objectives."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"## The eleven tools"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"| Tool | Purpose |"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"| `task_list` | List coordination-visible tasks with stable session ids, status, titles, todo/goal p"},{"id":"p33s2","text":"rogress; filterable by `team`; `ungrouped: true` (0.19.0) lists only sessions belonging to NO worksp"},{"id":"p33s3","text":"ace — the remediation view for the ungrouped bucket, paired with `task_workspace` and the registry's"},{"id":"p33s4","text":" `expectedWorkspace` |
| `task_progress` | Read one task in depth: live/cold state, queued messages,"},{"id":"p33s5","text":" conversation tail, todos, goal |
| `task_send` | Deliver a visible follow-up prompt (`mode: queue` "},{"id":"p33s6","text":"or `steer`; `reference` links an earlier instruction); returns a `messageId` plus a `queueDepth` rec"},{"id":"p33s7","text":"eipt `{nextTurn, nextStep}` (post-send; one next-turn message is consumed per round, so depth N ≈ N "},{"id":"p33s8","text":"rounds before it is read) |
[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"### `/tasks` — the no-model fast lane"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"Read-only lookups can bypass the model entirely: `/tasks` (all tasks), `/tasks team <name>` (one wor"},{"id":"p35s2","text":"kstream), `/tasks <sessionId>` (one task's progress, short-id prefixes resolve when unique). The com"},{"id":"p35s3","text":"mand executes directly in the host — zero tokens, instant answer. Anything that *acts* (send/spawn/w"},{"id":"p35s4","text":"ait/cancel) still goes through the tools."},{"id":"p36s1","text":"### Copying session ids — one click in the session header"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"### Orchestration view — a live topology with the current session as supervisor (0.20.0, cards resto"},{"id":"p38s2","text":"ion view — a live topology with the current session as supervisor (0.20.0, cards restored in 0.22.0)"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}
